     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Greetings,<div><br><div>I am trying to check and correct for spatial autocorrelation in a SEM because the data are drawn from three distinct forests. The data file is attached (called BSAx.csv).</div><div><br></div><div>Here is code for a simple SEM from these data (to test the problem; the actual model will be more complex) and the spatial correction using spatialCorrect in semTools:</div><div><br></div><div>library(lavaan)</div><div>library(semTools)</div><div><br></div><div><div>BSAx &lt;- read.csv(&quot;./BSAx.csv&quot;, header=T)</div><div>head(BSAx)</div><div><br></div><div>smodelx &lt;- &#39;ncvs15 ~ ncvs12 + mpa14</div><div>ncvs12 ~ grpar345&#39;</div><div><br></div><div>sfitx &lt;- sem(smodelx, data=BSAx, meanstructure=T)</div><div>summary(sfitx, standardized=T, rsquare=T, fit.measures=T)</div><div><br></div><div>spatialCorrect(sfitx, BSAx$lat, BSAx$long, alpha = 0.05)    <br></div></div><div><br></div><div>When I run this, this is the (lack of) result:</div><div><div>$Morans_I</div><div>named list()</div><div><br></div><div>$parameters</div><div>named list()</div></div><div><br></div><div>I will greatly appreciate any insights.</div><div><br></div><div>- Janet</div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
